Warpkeep Assets — licensing map

Copyright 2026 Warpkeep contributors

Warpkeep-Assets is a mixed-license repository. No single license covers every
file or release attachment, and public availability does not by itself grant
permission to reuse an asset.

## Quick reference

| Material | License or status |
| --- | --- |
| Project-authored repository software in `scripts/`, `tests/`, and `.github/`, plus project-authored root configuration | Apache License 2.0 |
| Project-authored prose in `README.md`, this file, and `ASSET-LICENSES.md` | Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) |
| Models, images, audio, video, previews, source packages, release attachments, manifests, provenance records, and reports | The exact per-set entry in `ASSET-LICENSES.md` and its dated provenance record |
| Third-party or externally governed material | Its original terms; no Warpkeep license is implied |
| Warpkeep names, logos, Hegemony identity, official domains, accounts, and canonical deployment identity | No trademark or endorsement rights granted |

The Apache-2.0 license for repository software matches the active software
license in the main Warpkeep repository. Its complete text is in
`LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`.

CC BY 4.0 applies only where Warpkeep controls the relevant copyright and this
repository expressly identifies the material as CC-BY-4.0. It allows sharing
and adaptation, including commercially, with attribution, a license link, and
an indication of changes. Its complete text is in `LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt`.

An entry marked “public archival and repository/release distribution
authorized; no separate open-license grant asserted” is not CC BY 4.0 or
Apache-2.0. It records Warpkeep's authority to preserve and publish that named
deposit, but it does not grant the public a general right to redistribute,
adapt, sublicense, or use the material outside the recorded terms.

## How to determine the terms for an asset

1. Find the named set or release in `ASSET-LICENSES.md`.
2. Read its linked manifest and dated provenance record.
3. Follow the most specific recorded license boundary and preserve required
   attribution and notices.
4. If no open-license grant is explicit, do not infer one from a filename,
   repository path, runtime use, release attachment, or project association.

This map aligns with the main Warpkeep repository's forward-looking policy:
project-authored software uses Apache-2.0, and authorized project-owned
creative work may use CC BY 4.0. It does not convert unresolved, third-party,
externally governed, or archive-only material into open content.

Main policy:

- https://github.com/ael-dev3/Warpkeep/blob/main/LICENSE
- https://github.com/ael-dev3/Warpkeep/blob/main/LICENSING.md
- https://github.com/ael-dev3/Warpkeep/blob/main/ASSETS-LICENSE.md

Nothing in this licensing map grants trademark rights or implies endorsement.
